    "narrative": "For tonight\u2019s slate, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (80.22) stands as our premier offensive anchor. Facing a favorable matchup against Liberatore, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a distinct platoon advantage and a premium spot in the two-hole, making him the highest-floor asset in our lineup. Close behind, **Cole Carrigg** (71.23) is our top UTIL play; he exploits a generous park factor and a weak SP matchup against Lugo, while his switch-hitting profile provides the versatility we prioritize in our 5x5 construction. **Gunnar Henderson** (68.30) and **Kyle Tucker** (64.50) also present strong value, with **Gunnar Henderson** overcoming a tough opponent in Wheeler thanks to an elite park environment that offsets the SP skill risk, and **Kyle Tucker** providing steady output against Bennett.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Luis Lara** (50.27). While he was a strong candidate given his switch-hitting ability and the favorable matchup against Ure\u00f1a, he ultimately fell short of the threshold compared to the high-upside deployments of **Nasim Nunez** (64.27) and **Jackson Merrill** (63.40). **Nasim Nunez** earns the start specifically for his efficiency against Ritchie, while **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a dynamic platoon edge that keeps his score firmly in the \"Strong\" territory. Conversely, we are aggressively managing our game caps by benching **Wade Meckler** (38.40) and **Denzer Guzman** (31.84); both players are strictly below our 40-point efficiency floor due to challenging matchups against the high-velocity Misiorowski.\n\nOperational risks today are primarily centered on our catching tandem. **Liam Hicks** (59.92) is in an advantageous spot against Stock, though his raw projection remains somewhat volatile compared to **Drake Baldwin** (51.78), who faces the stiffer challenge of Cavalli. We are also monitoring the speed-based upside of **Andy Pages** (63.49); his score is bolstered by a favorable SP delivery profile that invites stolen base opportunities, which remains our primary objective in this scarcity-driven league. No major weather alerts are pending, but we are keeping a close eye on the late-afternoon updates for any defensive shifts that might impact the batting order stability for **Sam Antonacci** and **Jorge Polanco**.",
